  (text "ESP32 controller, I2C mux/expander, RTC, NFC, buttons, fan, microSD, debug"
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 20 20 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 2 2))
      (justify left))
    (uuid "969c67fe-6406-54d1-bd25-5464a9c70ad1"))
  (text "X-42 shared interrupt PD_INT_N (IO34, level): 4x TPS26750 I2Ct_IRQ + both TCA9535 INT. Firmware drain-all: on low, read the IRQ status of all 4 PD controllers and both expander input ports (each read clears its source) and repeat until the line is high; never stop at the first source found. Poll all six once after every ESP32 reset."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 20 23.5 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.5 1.5))
      (justify left))
    (uuid "ea276a4b-33b8-5954-825e-d53d94a1681b"))
  (text "X-42 shared interrupt CHG_INT_N (IO35, 256 us pulses): every BQ25756 ~INT on the line. On a falling edge read FAULT/FLAG of every BQ25756 on it; also poll them every 1 s and after reset (overlapping pulses merge). Latch safety faults in firmware until acknowledged."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 20 27 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.5 1.5))
      (justify left))
    (uuid "6b41912e-d2fb-5c3c-b4fa-80d6faef209d"))
  (text "Mux channels 0-3 are no longer used by the USB-C ports (their BQ25756s moved to each TPS26750 I2Cc bus); they keep pull-ups and test pads as spare/debug branches."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 20 30.5 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.5 1.5))
      (justify left))
    (uuid "3f6d9810-80e8-56ab-8a75-978ae4c61608"))
